id: SCA-077
title: Dockerfile secret in build argument
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: Dockerfile
  extensions: .dockerfile
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: ARG\s+(PASSWORD|SECRET|TOKEN|API_KEY|PRIVATE_KEY|AWS_SECRET|DB_PASSWORD)
    message: ARG values are stored in image layer metadata. Secrets passed as build args are recoverable by anyone with access to the image.
fix: Use BuildKit secrets — RUN --mount=type=secret,id=mysecret. Never pass secrets as build arguments.
